# Build context exclusions.
#
# Both Python images end with `COPY . .`, and without this file that copies the
# entire working tree into the build context - including data/ (BigEarthNet
# shards, SECOND, the CDVQA mirror: tens of gigabytes), checkpoints/, models/
# and .git. A verification build was still transferring context after eleven
# minutes and 7.6 GB when this was written.
#
# Nothing excluded here is *needed* in the image: docker-compose mounts
# ./models and ./data as volumes at runtime, so baking them in would ship a
# second, stale copy of data the container is about to have mounted over it.

# Datasets and trained weights - mounted as volumes, never baked in.
data/
checkpoints/
checkpoints_backup/
models/

# Runtime output: gitignored already, and meaningless inside a fresh image.
artifacts/
*.db
satquery_runs.db

# Version control and local tooling.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.claude/
.venv/
venv/

# Python build and cache artifacts.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# The frontend has its own image and its own build context (context: frontend
# in docker-compose.yml), so its dependencies must not travel in the API
# context - node_modules alone is hundreds of megabytes.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.next/
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Tests and their fixtures are not part of a serving image.
tests/

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
